{"id": "EUVD-2026-86767", "enisaUuid": "8aaf85d6-5d67-31da-bbb6-1d6fa5a5bc09", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel: ethosu: Ensure cmd stream ends with a stop op\n\nWhile the QSIZE register setting should prevent an out of bounds access\nof the command stream, it is not clear whether the h/w generates an\ninterrupt in this case as is required (to prevent a timeout). As a stop op\nis expected end of the command stream, let's just ensure it is present. A\nstop op in the middle of the command stream also makes no sense.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf957f166f7ba548034db2a10e63f71df97f12e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb3a41fd35e352fba387c4320a1fa0352f3e551c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97913", "GHSA-3g6x-42f6-fgw4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "57aecae7-50f4-386a-b621-441359c2e4f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "724f27b5-6cac-316a-b6a0-f01bbb5f1e30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "8fa12572-53fd-3dd5-b97b-9efa910a0f60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a5e9c0228e613f0ef2a58b9782d7c0ea8f1e58b <bf957f166f7ba548034db2a10e63f71df97f12e2"}, {"id": "d315bccd-44a1-34d1-bd5b-ac609f0e3558", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d92bcfa0-7a5a-341d-9d7e-6608aff446b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e65e1fef-8669-33e1-934f-3062f07f2cc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a5e9c0228e613f0ef2a58b9782d7c0ea8f1e58b <eb3a41fd35e352fba387c4320a1fa0352f3e551c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f0686d7b-6631-3b24-ab18-6ffe12696547", "v